cff-version: "1.2.0"
title: "TIR-CMM — Threat-Informed Response Capability Maturity Model"
message: "If you use TIR-CMM in research, assessment, assurance or professional work, please cite the canonical model."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Adineh
    given-names: Reza
    website: "https://rezaadineh.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ReZaAdineH/tir-cmm"
url: "https://tir-cmm.com"
abstract: >-
  A threat-informed response capability maturity model that measures whether an
  organisation can act on a detected attack inside adversary breakout time, with
  sufficient authority and evidence that the response capability works. TIR-CMM
  contains eight domains, 58 sub-capabilities, an 8x8 Containment Lattice and
  seven numbered constraint families implemented as eight checks in v1.0, and
  is the response measurement companion to
  TID-CMM within the UTIOM ecosystem.
keywords:
  - incident response
  - response engineering
  - containment
  - cyber incident response
  - response maturity
  - threat-informed response
  - containment margin
  - MTTDecide
  - security operations
  - UTIOM
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-24"
